      "summary": "The setting moves from overwhelming enemies and their denial of divine help to protection, answered prayer, sleep and renewed confidence, an urgent rescue appeal, and blessing for God's people. Repetition makes protection, surrounding danger, and divine help its principal hooks. Mushrooms, thunder, grounded feet, successive slaps, a fist, and clothing intensify the imagery. Significant shifts include losing God as the speaker's honor, leaving divine sustaining unstated, and turning accomplished blows against enemies into a demand for blows. The untranslated heading removes the explicit David–Absalom frame from the sung text.",
